# Tool catalog

One line per tool. Whoever adds a tool adds its line here. The commands below are placeholders: replace them with the real ones.

| Tool | What it does | How to call | Used by |
|---|---|---|---|
| RPC relay | All chain reads (JSON-RPC over HTTP), nine chains. Lanes live > paper > research, each with a daily Alchemy budget, then public nodes (`GET $RPC_RELAY_URL/health` = today's spend; budget spent → public-node range/depth limits surface as `all providers failed`). Read-only methods only (sending is the gate's job), incl. `debug_trace*`, `trace_block`, `alchemy_getAssetTransfers` (40-1000 CU; valid categories `external internal erc20 erc721 erc1155 specialnft`); state diffs: `prestateTracer` + `diffMode`. Calldata: `eth_getTransactionByHash`. Ethereum receipts may be `null` for older txs: use `eth_getLogs` on the block + `transactionHash`. `eth_getLogs`: ≤32 addresses per call; never pad `topics` with extra `null` slots (silent `[]`); >10000 logs → shrink the range; "odd number of digits"/"odd length" = your hex is mistyped (addresses 40 digits, topics 64); `-32700` = malformed JSON body. Caps: bsc ≤5000-block ranges, topic-only ≤1000 (≤125 at head), public node has no getLogs (costs CU); elysium, avalanche ≤10000; arbitrum topic-only ≤30000, `trace_block` fails; responses >32 MiB refused; no `trace_*` on polygon/hyperevm; base is 0.2 s/block since 11-05 (time from timestamps: `pitfalls/base-block-time-0p2s.md`); elysium refuses `debug_*`/`trace_*`, address-less getLogs at head ≤2000 blocks (32 MiB), USDC `0xb47c4C8F73F009CC0C0d3f92B388d13E293F0B65`. On bsc/polygon a zero counts only with a same-run, same-shape, same-window control that returns logs (transient `[]` 11-10/11-11); file a relay bug only after `relay-probe` in the same minute. Blockscout listings can be empty for active contracts: cross-check with `eth_getLogs`; ethereum/arbitrum Blockscout API now asks keyless callers for X402 payment (use GitHub raw for source). Per-chain details, error texts, incident history: `wiki read infra/relay-reference.md` and `pitfalls/relay-getlogs-invalid-params.md` | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/rpc.py <chain> <method> '<json params>' [--lane research\|paper] [--params-file f] [--out f]` (read-only; prints the raw response, exit 1 on error; `--out` saves it and prints a count; refuses getLogs with non-hex bounds, wrong-length or near-miss hand-typed topics; stderr `hint:` on empty reverts/results and near-miss token addresses). The `curl "$RPC_RELAY_URL/..."` form is refused in "don't ask" sessions (11-12) | all |
| ledger | Pre-ingested events (liquidations and similar) on all nine chains (the built-in sources cover base/arbitrum/ethereum; the others start empty until someone runs `ledger add-source` there), refreshed every 15 min; `actor_daily` shows who is active. It is a head start, not the whole chain: anything else is one `eth_getLogs` away through the relay. `ledger sources` lists every tracked event incl. agent-added ones, table `cursors` shows each source's backfill (`next_block`). Agent-added amounts are principal, not profit (`wiki read infra/ledger-agent-sources.md`) | `ledger top --chain base --days 7` / `ledger query "<SQL>"` / `ledger query --json "<SQL>"` (one JSON object per row, no cell truncation, 50 rows) / `ledger sources` | earner, paper-reviewer, researcher |
| ledger add-source | Track a new event in the ledger yourself (no approval needed, bounded CU). Write the JSON spec to `scratch/`, then install it. `event` = full canonical signature; required `topic0` = its computed keccak (dynamic/tuple types allowed); `indexed` = the leading indexed params (max 3); `data` = only the static one-word params at the front of the non-indexed ones; interleaved events: `actor_field: tx_from`, nothing in `indexed`; ≤20 addresses per chain. Check `cursors` within ~2 ticks; backfill takes hours (ethereum) to a day+ (arbitrum, elysium); zero events count only once `tools/ledger-source-coverage.py` shows the cursor at the head. Details: `wiki read infra/relay-reference.md` | `ledger add-source scratch/<name>.json` | earner, researcher |
| feed | `farm-feed` long-poll: a bot waits for one event instead of polling (`/head` is off). Re-read via relay on `gap`/429/503, keep a 5-10 min safety poll, no busy events; per-filter 150k, total 700k CU/day; `/health` `cu_today` adds to daily CU. Details: `wiki read infra/feed.md` | from bot code: `GET http://127.0.0.1:8546/logs/<chain>?address=<a>&topic0=<hash>&after=<cursor>&timeout=55`; by hand: `scratch/feed-probe/feed_probe.py` (shell `curl` may be refused) | earner, paper bots, live bots |
| simulate | Dry-run a transaction: `eth_call` (revert / return) or `debug_traceCall` (full trace) through the relay, against `latest`. For stateful multi-call measurements use the shared local fork listed below | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/rpc.py <chain> eth_call '[{"from":"0x..","to":"0x..","data":"0x.."},"latest"]'` | earner, paper-reviewer |
| KB schema | Tables and columns of the knowledge base | `kb schema` | all |
| KB query | Read-only SQL; at most 50 rows, 10 s. Table output cuts cells at 400 chars (ending `...`); `--json` prints one JSON object per row with no cut. Read a long field with `--json` before any `kb update` of it, never from a cut read (recover from `revisions.before`) | `kb query "SELECT ... WHERE ... LIMIT 20"` / `kb query --json "SELECT ..."` | all |
| KB write | Validated insert / update; records author and run; rejects duplicates with the existing id; key fields (e.g. `protocols.protocol`, `leads.target`) can't be changed. `protocol` names are lowercase with underscores (`aave_v4`, `gearbox_v3`): before adding, `kb query` both the hyphen and underscore spellings. A parse error near the end of a long argument (`Expecting ',' delimiter` at your text's length) = the shell cut it: use `kb-file` below | `kb add <table> '<json>'` / `kb update <table> <id> '<json>'` | all |
| kb-file | `kb add` / `kb update` with the JSON object read from a file (write it with the Write tool), so long values with quotes or apostrophes never pass through shell quoting; same validation and author recording, prints length + tail on a parse error. Use it for any value over ~300 chars | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/kb-file.py add <table> --file scratch/<name>.json` / `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/kb-file.py update <table> <id> --file scratch/<name>.json` | all |
| wiki search | Ranked matches: path, type, updated, first line (max 20) | `wiki search "<terms>" --limit 10` | all |
| wiki read | Full page | `wiki read <path>` | all |
| wiki history | Recent commits for a page | `wiki history <path>` | all |
| wiki write | Write a page from a draft file and commit it | `wiki write <path> -m "<message>" --file scratch/<draft>.md` | all |
| bot archive | Stopped bots with their code, manifest and `ARCHIVE.md` (reason). Search with grep | `grep -ril "<term>" bots/archive/*/manifest.yaml` then read the directory | earner, meta |
| signer (from inside a live bot only) | Unix socket `$SIGNER_SOCK`: `{"op":"send",...}` → signed + broadcast after policy; `{"op":"limits"}` shows what is allowed today | `/opt/farm/lib/farmbot_signer.py` | live bots |
| fork | Local anvil fork of each mainnet (base 9001, arbitrum 9002, ethereum 9003, bsc 9004, polygon 9005, avalanche 9006, optimism 9007, hyperevm 9008, elysium 9009 (reset/replay there mine one extra block: fork at `<block>+1`), forked from the relay's research lane. Fake funds, impersonation, deploys, replays. Shared: take `fork lease <chain> <min≤60> [note]` first (blocks others' `reset`/`replay`; `--force` overrides, note it), `fork release <chain>` when done; if `fork status` generation changed during a measurement, discard it. Do reset→deploy→fund→guard→success in one script (`wiki read pitfalls/shared-fork-concurrency.md`). hyperevm: every tx incl. the deploy < 2,000,000 gas. Anvil: only callTracer works; `eth_getStorageAt` ≤400 slots per request. Details: `wiki read infra/relay-reference.md` | `fork status` / `fork lease <chain> <min> [note]` / `fork release <chain>` / `fork reset <chain> [block]` / `fork fund <chain> <addr> <eth>` / `fork fund-token <chain> <token> <holder> <to> <amount>` (`FAILED`, exit 2 = pick another holder) / `fork deploy <chain> <bytecode.hex|out/X.sol/X.json> [--args <abi-encoded constructor args>]` (status 0 at ~intrinsic gas = missing args) / `fork call` / `fork send <chain> '<tx json>'` / `fork replay <chain> <txhash>` (re-forks!) / `fork trace <chain> <txhash>` / `fork url <chain>` | earner, paper-reviewer, researcher |
| forge | Solidity compiler and test runner (Foundry) for executor contracts. Work in `scratch/<bot>/contracts`; `forge test --fork-url $(fork url base)` runs tests against the fork | `/opt/foundry/bin/forge build` / `forge test` / `cast` for ABI encoding | earner, paper-reviewer |
| paper runner | Run a bot in `bots/paper/<id>/` as a supervised service (user farmbot, paper lane, no keys). `paper list` / `paper status <id>` / `paper logs <id>` (stdout/stderr only; a bot's own files are under `bots/paper/<id>/logs/`) | `paper start <id>` / `paper stop <id>` / `paper restart <id>` / `paper archive <id> --reason "<why>"` | earner, paper-reviewer (archive), live-operator |
| gate | Deploy gate (holds keys; enforces X=2000, n=200/day, L=50 USD at signing-time price, cap 400/bot). Promotes on all nine chains; a first promote on a chain is refused until the human deposits native gas (and USDC if `principal_usdc`) in that chain's intermediate wallet (`gate status` shows holdings): roles that may write `inbox/human/` ask there, earner/paper-reviewer write `inbox/meta/` (meta forwards). 18 USD gas-wallet cap on base and optimism; bsc USDC has 18 decimals; hyperevm tx ≤2,000,000 gas; elysium gas priced by HyperEVM's feed. `status` shows capital, today's loss, frozen flag, every live bot's address/balances/nonces. `stop`/`sweep` exit 3 = sweep incomplete: funds not all back, still counts toward X, rerun later, never report it as swept. `fund` refuses a top-up past 400 USD; executor bots must read `EXECUTOR_ADDR`/`state/executor.json` or `promote` refuses. Details: `wiki read infra/relay-reference.md` | `gate status [id]` / `gate promote <id>` / `gate fund <id> <usd>` / `gate restart <id>` / `gate stop <id>` / `gate stop --all` | paper-reviewer (promote), live-operator (all), earner/meta (status) |
| X feed | Not available yet. If posts from specific accounts would help, the researcher proposes a feed (cost, accounts) in `inbox/human/` | — | researcher |
| DefiLlama | Public API, no key: protocols, TVL, yields. Filter with `jq`; responses are large | `curl -s https://api.llama.fi/protocols \| jq '[.[] \| select(.chains[]? == "Base")] \| length'` / `curl -s https://yields.llama.fi/pools` | earner, researcher |
| web | Fetch: harness built-in. Search: local keyless metasearch (GitHub, Stack Overflow, HN, arXiv, Wikipedia, npm, crates.io; weak on the general web); `!gh` searches GitHub repos only (find deployment lists/addresses). Short plain terms work best: hyphenated or long queries often return `(no results)`; `--json` ignores `-n` (~40 KB). Earner `web_search` uses the same backend; if it errors, run the `websearch` CLI from the shell. No CAPTCHA/429 evasion, no bulk search loops; if thin, web_fetch DefiLlama adapters, docs or the explorer | `websearch "<terms>" [-n N] [--time day\|week\|month\|year] [--json]` / `websearch "!gh <terms>" -n 5` | all |
| relay-log-scan | Bounded research-only log export through the relay: small pages, automatic <=32-address batches (one shared request cap; audit records each batch), adaptive address bisection on explicit smaller provider caps and scalar fallback on Variadic array rejection, size-error splitting, transient backoff, request cap, audit, no export on incomplete scan; rejects topics that silently match nothing (non-32-byte hashes such as 4-byte selectors, trailing `null` slots unless `--keep-trailing-nulls`). Requires an address (no topic-only scans: call `eth_getLogs` directly for those). Research diagnostic only; bots remain self-contained. `--chain` accepts all nine chains. | `python3 tools/relay-log-scan.py --chain base --filter scratch/filter.json --from-block 100 --to-block 200 --max-requests 24 --output scratch/logs.json --audit scratch/log-audit.json` (new output paths; default page 2000 blocks) | researcher, earner, paper-reviewer |
| relay-probe | Reproduce a suspected relay quirk with a same-run control before filing it (≤5 research-lane calls). `getlogs-topic-only`: one block's Transfer logs address-less vs address-filtered (USDC and the block's busiest emitter); `getlogs-range`: USDC Transfer over 8 blocks, address+topics+fromBlock/toBlock vs no-topics filtered client-side (`--from-block N` for a historical range). Counts must match. All nine chains (elysium's 8 blocks are ~1 s, so 0=0 is normal there); 0 on both sides = quiet range, retry with `--from-block` | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/relay-probe.py getlogs-topic-only --chain ethereum` / `... getlogs-range --chain ethereum [--from-block N]` | meta, researcher, earner |
| manifest-check | Static check of a paper manifest's deployment fields, no RPC: `executor` is exactly one existing `.json` artifact path, `executor_args` is 0x-hex with one word per static constructor input (`{bot}` = the gate fills in the bot's address; a fixed `owner` address arg and an `EXECUTOR_ADDR` fallback to a hard-coded address are warned), an executor bot's code mentions `EXECUTOR_ADDR` or `executor.json`, `allowed_contracts` are addresses (`[]` is correct for an executor bot), capital/loss caps, required fields, and `capital_usd` / `max_loss_per_tx_usd` lines are bare numbers (no inline `# comment`). Exit 1 on any ERROR. Not a safety review | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/manifest-check.py bots/paper/<id>/manifest.yaml` / `... --all` | earner, paper-reviewer, meta |
| workspace history | `/srv/farm/ws` is not a git repo. Per-run snapshots of the workspace live in `/srv/farm/ws/history` (one commit per run, made by the harness; agents cannot commit), the wiki has its own repo. Read-only | `git -C /srv/farm/ws/history log\|show\|diff` / `git -C /srv/farm/ws/wiki log\|show\|diff` | meta, all |
| researcher-funnel | Per-instance researcher lead funnel (human 2026-11-09 two-researchers): leads added, non-liquidation, earner-touched alive / dead_end, named in a bot manifest. Read-only on the KB; heuristic, check `--rows` before quoting | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/researcher-funnel.py [--since 2026-11-09] [--rows]` | meta, researcher |
| session-report | Append your session report line safely: validates fields and role outcome, rejects duplicate run_id (so append once, as the very last step, after all KB/wiki writes), opens the day file with O_APPEND (never rewrites it, unlike Write/Edit). `coverage` lists runs with KB attempts but no report. If the tool errors, append the line the old way and note it in `inbox/meta/` | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/session-report.py append --file /srv/farm/ws/scratch/report-<run_id>.json` / `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/session-report.py coverage --date 2026-11-04` | all |
| prompt-size | Assembled prompt bytes per role (common + role + TOOLS.md); limit 60000, keep ≤56000. Run after every edit of a role file or TOOLS.md; exit 1 if over | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/prompt-size.py` | meta, researcher |
| wiki-eval | Retrieval eval for `wiki search`: questions in `tools/wiki-eval/questions.jsonl` (query + page that answers it); prints hit@1/3/5, MRR, tokens per query and misses. Add a row when you failed to find a page that existed | `python3 /srv/farm/ws/tools/wiki-eval/run.py [--json scratch/<out>.json]` | meta, researcher |
| agent-added ledger sources | Index of what each agent-added source tracks and its units (Curve fee-forward and PegKeeper, Beefy, Liquity V2, Olympus, Alchemix v3, Yearn auctions, Concentrator, Reserve). Amounts are principal or raw units, never profit. Adding a source? Add its row to that page, not a line here | `wiki read infra/ledger-agent-sources.md` | researcher, earner |
| ledger-source-coverage | Read-only comparison of workspace agent source specs with paginated ledger cursors; reports configured/initialized/verified counts and missing emitters per chain. No RPC; no claim of head catch-up or complete historical backfill. | `python3 tools/ledger-source-coverage.py [--source <source_id>] [--json]` / `wiki read infra/ledger-source-coverage.md` | all |
